# Wave H.l.b — Operator datetime chrome

## Problem

After H.l (`data-operator-surface`), shared datetime chrome still leaked Denali vocabulary:

- CSS/BEM: `denali-time-picker*`, `denali-wizard-time-picker*`
- DOM: `data-denali-wizard-time-picker`, `data-denali-time-picker`, `data-operator-wizard-calendar*`
- Shell imports: `DenaliTimeInput`, `DenaliWizardDatetimePicker` from generated operator-ui bindings

Wizard create/edit and settings date/time flows all hit these hooks — including `@app-tour/workspace-denali` `DenaliTimeInput` (primary path via bindings).

## Decision

1. Rename **time/calendar chrome** class + data attributes to `operator-*` / `data-operator-*` in:
   - `packages/workspaces/denali` time input + time panel (product SoT for picker UI)
   - `apps/web/src/components/{i18n,ui}` shell copies
2. Update Denali theme CSS (`wizard-calendar.css`, `wizard-fields.css`) to the new selectors (no dual legacy — E2E/scripts updated in lockstep).
3. Codegen operator-ui bindings: export **`WorkspaceTimeInput`** / **`WorkspaceWizardDatetimePicker`** as canonical shell names; keep `DenaliTimeInput` / `DenaliWizardDatetimePicker` as **deprecated aliases** (same component) for one wave.
4. Shell `localized-datetime-picker.tsx` imports the Workspace* names.

## Out of scope

- ~~Renaming `denali-wizard-datetime` / `denali-date-picker` BEM~~ → **done in** [`wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.mdoc`](./wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.mdoc) (Wave H.p)
- Broader wizard BEM (composite / review / pickers)
- Removing `apps/web/src/wizard/denali/*` firewall
- Install-graph isolation

## Verify

```bash
rg 'data-denali-wizard-time-picker|denali-time-picker' apps/web/src/components packages/workspaces/denali/src/ui/components/time packages/workspaces/denali/src/ui/components/denali-time-input.tsx
# expect empty (or only comments)
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm --filter @app-tour/workspace-denali run build
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-h-operator-datetime-chrome.spec.ts \
  test/denali-wizard-theme.spec.ts
```
